t calls withConfig on the cached raw schema with the new config, returning a different configured instance.', 'description': 'Ensures that the cache stores the un‑configured schema and that each call can apply a distinct configuration.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'schemaUri', 'value': 'new TestSchemaLocation("http://example.com/multi-config")'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'new SchemaValidatorsConfig().setFailFast(true)'}], 'expected': 'Same as previous case – getMappedSchema is NOT called again; withConfig is invoked with the new config, producing a different JsonSchema object.', 'description': 'Second invocation with a different config validates that withConfig is applied per call.'}]}, {'group': 'Cache Disabled – Multiple Sequential Calls', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'schemaUri', 'value': 'new TestSchemaLocation("http://example.com/no-cache-multi")'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'new SchemaValidatorsConfig()'}], 'expected': 'getMappedSchema is invoked on each call (twice for two sequential invocations); no caching occurs, and the returned schemas are the raw results from getMappedSchema (no withConfig call).', 'description': 'Confirms that disabling the cache forces a fresh mapping for every request.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'schemaUri', 'value': 'new TestSchemaLocation("http://example.com/no-cache-multi")'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'new SchemaValidatorsConfig()'}], 'expected': 'Same as previous – getMappedSchema called again; the two returned JsonSchema instances are distinct.', 'description': 'Second sequential call should still bypass any cache.'}]}, {'group': 'Cache Key Sensitivity – Fragment Identifier', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'schemaUri', 'value': 'new TestSchemaLocation("http://example.com/schema#fragmentA")'}, {'parameter': 'config', 'value': 'new SchemaValidatorsConfig()'}], 'expected': "When caching is enabled, a schema with fragment '#fragmentA' is cached under its full URI; a later request with '#fragmentB' is